<title>SINGAPORE: Kay Hian posts flat 1996 net profit.</title>
<headline>Kay Hian posts flat 1996 net profit.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			42.78  vs    42.62</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)		 5.75  vs     5.75</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		9.74  vs     9.70</p>
<p>    Turnover			 121.74  vs   115.91</p>
<p>    Other income		     1.58  vs     3.54</p>
<p>    Interest expense		 4.06  vs     3.29</p>
<p>    Operating pretax profit     47.42  vs    53.85</p>
<p>    Associates			10.47  vs     4.84</p>
<p>    Tax				 15.11  vs    16.07</p>
<p>    Dividend pay date:	    22 July 1997</p>
<p>    Last date books open:	  7 July 1997</p>
<p>Note - Stockbroker Kay Hian Holdings Ltd said apart form strong performance in early 1996, the rest of the year was lacklustre due to numerous global and regional uncertainties.</p>
<p>--Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
</text>
